{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing","id":1261337,"title":"I thought they Abandoned the whole Space is the Umbra Thing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-18T11:45:52-07:00","id":1261337,"title":"I thought they Abandoned the whole Space is the Umbra Thing?","content":"Did I just imagine it or didn\u2019t revised abandon the Idea that Space was the Umbra? How does it make sense to use it, for one if it\u2019s true it makes mage way waaay more different then the other games. Why don\u2019t Earth telescopes notice all the Umbra shenanigans? I get that they are doing the whole before the World was mapped it wasn\u2019t round thing but it\u2019s silly to have everything be immaterial in space, or past the Asteroid Belt! I mean so that means what comets become material at a certain point but revert back to emphemera during their predictable cycles? Why don\u2019t we see spirits then? Why does the observable universe act like it isn\u2019t spirit stuff?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s just really silly... I mean it would be enough to say the Gauntlet is very low, or non existent but the two planes are still two different dimensions.<br /> <br /> What is the consequences then for say Gavin spirits materialize in space in a live broadcast, or for Astronomers?<br /> <br /> Is the bubble of material growing as we visit more of space? So colonies will convert things to material? If that is the case why wouldn\u2019t the technocracy just jump in and colonize things before the rest of the world? Who could stop them?<br /> <br /> Can anyone sell me on Space is the Umbra, because I thought they was either downplayed or outright abandoned by the time we got to the revised core/Infinite Tapestry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T12:25:37-07:00","id":1261345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I just imagine it or didn\u2019t revised abandon the Idea that Space was the Umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Or rather, yep, to some extent. They abandoned that idea in Werewolf, but not in Mage.<br /> <br /> In Mage both Infinite Tapestry and VE: Convention Book (the last being the final book of Revised era) state that outer space extends to the asteroid belt and little more. Before outer space extended at least to Pluto, possibly forever (it wasn't clearly defined). So in revised there's less outer space than before for Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does it make sense to use it, for one if it\u2019s true it makes mage way waaay more different then the other games. Why don\u2019t Earth telescopes notice all the Umbra shenanigans? I get that they are doing the whole before the World was mapped it wasn\u2019t round thing but it\u2019s silly to have everything be immaterial in space, or past the Asteroid Belt! I mean so that means what comets become material at a certain point but revert back to emphemera during their predictable cycles? Why don\u2019t we see spirits then? Why does the observable universe act like it isn\u2019t spirit stuff?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s just really silly... I mean it would be enough to say the Gauntlet is very low, or non existent but the two planes are still two different dimensions.<br /> <br /> What is the consequences then for say Gavin spirits materialize in space in a live broadcast, or for Astronomers? </div> </div> </div>The explanation given it's a phenomena VE call the Tegmar Lensing. It's an illusion that prevents astronomers from seing weirdness beyond the Asteroid Belt. So...Astronomers see what they want to see. Telescopes only work up to a point, which got reduced after the Avatar Storm, and after that it's all an illusion that's coherent with belief but not solid enough to carve matter by itself.<br /> <br /> What happens with comets I don'0t know...I guess that dematerialize and/or become illusory after a point<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is the bubble of material growing as we visit more of space? So colonies will convert things to material? </div> </div> </div>Yes, human experience expands the territory.<br /> <br /> Even unmanned probes have a little effect as long as they're monitored by humans. Satelites and such create small roads and bubbles of Conventional Space where they travel, but those bubbles don't extend a lot. In that sense there is material outer space outside the Asteroid Belt, but rather than a vast expanse it's a sort of slice or road.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that is the case why wouldn\u2019t the technocracy just jump in and colonize things before the rest of the world? Who could stop them? </div> </div> </div>Well, they try, but the Umbra it's kinda dangerous. Cue the Avatar Storm erasing more than half the Outer Space they managed to build there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can anyone sell me on Space is the Umbra, because I thought they was either downplayed or outright abandoned by the time we got to the revised core/Infinite Tapestry? </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to sell that, that's work for someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-18-2018, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T12:49:54-07:00","id":1261353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing#post1261337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can anyone sell me on Space is the Umbra, because I thought they was either downplayed or outright abandoned by the time we got to the revised core/Infinite Tapestry?</div> </div> </div> </div>This bothers me too. The closest I could come up with is that all Mages are very slightly a shallowing and that far enough out, the gauntlet is so thin that the awakened automatically fall through. A sleeper would never encounter a Deep Umbra horror as their unbelief is strong enough to keep them on this side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T13:43:41-07:00","id":1261372,"title":"","content":"That would be a decent way of solving it if the authors chose to change their stance in the future. It only requires the VE to be wrong, and they really could be. It's not like normal humans travel to the stars very often (not without mage help anyway).<br /> <br /> I'm more brute and would just ignore it, but to each his own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T14:38:49-07:00","id":1261389,"title":"","content":"It has the same inherent problems of Dark ages saying the world would change shape with the belief of humans(ignoring that humans knew the earth was round long before Columbus and his spiel was that he thought the earth was smaller than it really was. Which the governing powers at that time knew as well, they gave him the boat to shut him up.)<br /> <br /> If the setting is actually malleable to such an extent it makes the modern WoD incredibly unlikely. To the extent of &quot;breaking suspension of disbelief the way a Mary Sue would&quot; unlikely. To mold such a chaotic environment into the an order to parallel our own world would require mages to force it that way and then get people to believe it works that way to get it to stick. A horrifying task considering that a non-round world would present evidence that it isn't round to the observant, preventing a prevailing belief that the earth is round, and thus creating an environment that does to mages trying to &quot;force it into a round shape&quot; what &quot;trying to move the moon&quot; has been known to do to modern technocrats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T15:43:41-07:00","id":1261409,"title":"","content":"Since the Book of Worlds, conventional space - our familiarspace, of lifeless rocks in a vast void - has existed in Mage. It's Earthrealm space, on our side of the Gauntlet. We don't see Umbral shenanigans with our Earth telescopes for the same reason you don't see spirits when you look through binoculars or a microscope on Earth.<br /> <br /> In Mage, beyond the Horizon, the barrier between Realms is so thin as to be nonexistent, but Sleeper space exploration extends the Gauntlet into new territory. This doesn't so much &quot;extend&quot; conventional space (Realms are of arbitrary size) as create more areas in which conventional space is separated from other Realms. The Horizon experience isn't substantially different than a videre.<br /> <br /> (I think the thing that people get hung up on is that BoW treats the Earthrealm as just another Realm.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T17:43:19-07:00","id":1261442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261409#post1261409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Book of Worlds, conventional space - our familiarspace, of lifeless rocks in a vast void - has existed in Mage. It's Earthrealm space, on our side of the Gauntlet. We don't see Umbral shenanigans with our Earth telescopes for the same reason you don't see spirits when you look through binoculars or a microscope on Earth.<br /> <br /> In Mage, beyond the Horizon, the barrier between Realms is so thin as to be nonexistent, but Sleeper space exploration extends the Gauntlet into new territory. This doesn't so much \u201cextend\u201d conventional space (Realms are of arbitrary size) as create more areas in which conventional space is separated from other Realms. The Horizon experience isn't substantially different than a videre.<br /> <br /> (I think the thing that people get hung up on is that BoW treats the Earthrealm as just another Realm.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give some page citations for this? I've been going through Book of Worlds, and so far it still seems to be supporting the notion that Conventional Space only exists within the Horizon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T18:00:28-07:00","id":1261444,"title":"","content":"Hmm, my language may be somewhat inexact here - I think we could say that our (material)<i> space </i>exists beyond the Horizon, but capital-C Conventional space doesn't?<br /> <br /> Do you take &quot;Conventional Space&quot; to be &quot;Earthrealm space with a Gauntlet&quot;, or are we talking about Earthrealm (&quot;material existence&quot;)?<br /> <br /> I would take &quot;Realspace becomes indistinguishable from Etherspace&quot; (pg 148) to mean that the various otherworld layers are united, not that Realspace <i>stops. </i>Obviously, if Conventional Space is defined as &quot;Earthrealm space with a Gauntlet&quot;, then it necessary ends wherever the Gauntlet does, but that's not the end of the Earthrealm, right?<br /> <br /> Would you disagree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T19:06:50-07:00","id":1261460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261389#post1261389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has the same inherent problems of Dark ages saying the world would change shape with the belief of humans(ignoring that humans knew the earth was round long before Columbus and his spiel was that he thought the earth was smaller than it really was. Which the governing powers at that time knew as well, they gave him the boat to shut him up.)<br /> <br /> If the setting is actually malleable to such an extent it makes the modern WoD incredibly unlikely. To the extent of &quot;breaking suspension of disbelief the way a Mary Sue would&quot; unlikely. To mold such a chaotic environment into the an order to parallel our own world would require mages to force it that way and then get people to believe it works that way to get it to stick. A horrifying task considering that a non-round world would present evidence that it isn't round to the observant, preventing a prevailing belief that the earth is round, and thus creating an environment that does to mages trying to &quot;force it into a round shape&quot; what &quot;trying to move the moon&quot; has been known to do to modern technocrats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the World of Darkness isn't our world. And the vast majority of people in the World of Darkness are ignorant Sheeple who really are that stupid that a handful of Order of Reason Mages can reshape the entire planet without anyone noticing any different one discovery at a time. Because that's the attitude the counterculture loving hippies at White Wolf had about the vast majority of people. That there are a few 'enlightened' who know what 'The Man' is up to, but most are just braindead idiots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T05:09:49-07:00","id":1261530,"title":"","content":"I, myself, ignore all this weird and solipsistic way of understanding the universe as WW tries so hard to enforce. Humanity is not that central in the great scheme of things, but It is an important force for belief has much power displayed as that of gods. <br /> <br /> Therefore to ME, there is a material universe out there with planets and who knows what else, they may not have a massive gauntlent as Earth has because only here we have so much channeled energy focused on such massive interdimensional/spiritual barrier. The universe is not the Umbra, i think thats really silly and kills the main fun of both traveling on unknow places on an infinite universe as it would kill the idea of a spiritual journey in the &quot;realms beyond this one&quot;. <br /> <br /> I dont even know why WW even had to try making them the same thing, it is all but a really lazy way of &quot;we dont wanna make an alien game anymore&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T06:53:17-07:00","id":1261550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261444#post1261444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, my language may be somewhat inexact here - I think we could say that our (material)<i> space </i>exists beyond the Horizon, but capital-C Conventional space doesn't?<br /> <br /> Do you take &quot;Conventional Space&quot; to be &quot;Earthrealm space with a Gauntlet&quot;, or are we talking about Earthrealm (&quot;material existence&quot;)?<br /> <br /> I would take &quot;Realspace becomes indistinguishable from Etherspace&quot; (pg 148) to mean that the various otherworld layers are united, not that Realspace <i>stops. </i>Obviously, if Conventional Space is defined as &quot;Earthrealm space with a Gauntlet&quot;, then it necessary ends wherever the Gauntlet does, but that's not the end of the Earthrealm, right?<br /> <br /> Would you disagree?</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of the question of what happens when a human on Earth uses a telescope to look into the Deep Universe, it's a moot point: if \u201cRealspace\u201d and \u201cEtherspace\u201d are indistinguishable beyond the Horizon, and there's no Gauntlet separating them, then there would seem to be no reason why, say, a telescope pointed at the moons of Jupiter shouldn't see Umbrood and the like living there. <br /> <br /> Then there's the more pressing question that the Book of Worlds doesn't, to my knowledge, address: is there anything preventing you from using Correspondence to teleport to the moons of Jupiter? Book of Worlds assumes that in order to go beyond the Horizon, you need to use Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022; Correspondence doesn't appear to be a viable way to bypass that. And to me, the best definition of Conventional Space is based on how Correspondence works: as long as Correspondence continues to work like it does on Earth, you're still dealing with Conventional Space; once it stops working normally, you're no longer dealing with Conventional Space. <br /> <br /> Also, Book of Worlds and even Infinite Tapestry are now out of date. The most current information is in the Revised Void Engineers Convention Book and in M20. In both sources, Conventional Space is described as extending out to the Asteroid Belt and then stopping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T07:53:51-07:00","id":1261560,"title":"","content":"If Tegmark lensing is what edits out unnatural phenomena ... why have Sleeper telescopes not determined that Alpha Centauri (former location of the Cop) is now a black hole? Since that was a thing that happened with the Avatar Storm in 1999, and Alpha Centauri is only 4 LY away ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T08:18:01-07:00","id":1261568,"title":"","content":"A black hole that is a Realm, caused by the Avatar Storm, inhabited by Threat Null - it's hardly a natural phenomena. Not any more than the COP itself was anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T08:52:48-07:00","id":1261575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261550#post1261550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of the question of what happens when a human on Earth uses a telescope to look into the Deep Universe, it's a moot point: if \u201cRealspace\u201d and \u201cEtherspace\u201d are indistinguishable beyond the Horizon, and there's no Gauntlet separating them, then there would seem to be no reason why, say, a telescope pointed at the moons of Jupiter shouldn't see Umbrood and the like living there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enh - Tegmark lensing was <i>probably </i>a necessary development to definitively make sure that this wasn't the case, but I think we already knew that Sleeper viewing devices can't see past Realm boundaries.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Realms are intermingled beyond the Horizon seems irrelevant if the telescope (and/or observer) is separated from other Realms by the Gauntlet. It doesn't matter how big the sky is if you're looking up at it from the bottom of a well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261550#post1261550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there's the more pressing question that the Book of Worlds doesn't, to my knowledge, address: is there anything preventing you from using Correspondence to teleport to the moons of Jupiter?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Per CB:VE? The diagram shows the Anthropic Horizon - the extension of Conventional Space beyond the Spatial Horizon - passing Jupiter, so, yeah, you probably can.<br /> <br /> But I follow your argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261550#post1261550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Book of Worlds and even Infinite Tapestry are now out of date. The most current information is in the Revised Void Engineers Convention Book and in M20. In both sources, Conventional Space is described as extending out to the Asteroid Belt and then stopping.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if we're taking Conventional Space to be material space with a Gauntlet, I agree. I'm not convinced that material existence - the Earthrealm/Realspace - ends at the asteroid belt, though. I think that in the Horizon the various otherworlds intermingle, but that (for example) the Anthropic Horizon (see the diagram in CB:VE) isn't an &quot;extension&quot; of Realspace, but rather an extension of the Gauntlet that separates the various Realms.<br /> <br /> In other worlds, I think that <i>material </i>Neptune exists; it's Earthrealm Neptune, the thing we see in telescopes. It's not Umbral, but it's located someplace where (at the moment), no barrier separates the various Umbral and material layers of existence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T09:25:51-07:00","id":1261588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261575#post1261575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we already knew that Sleeper viewing devices can't see past Realm boundaries.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Realms are intermingled beyond the Horizon seems irrelevant if the telescope (and/or observer) is separated from other Realms by the Gauntlet. It doesn't matter how big the sky is if you're looking up at it from the bottom of a well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand your argument.<br /> <br /> Premise 1: Sleeper viewing devices can't see past Realm boundaries/Gauntlet<br /> <br /> Premise 2: Realms are intermingled beyond the Horizon (i.e: There are NO Realm boundaries/Gauntlet sepparating Matter and Spirit, or it's so thin it doesn't matter)<br /> <br /> The rational conclusion would be that telescopes CAN see the Umbra past Horizon because you've just said that those limits that normaly would prevent view don't apply there.<br /> <br /> If outer space and the Umbra are intermingled then there's no Gauntlet preventing me see that intermingled space because my sight it's paralel to what the Gauntlet it's sepparating. My sight traverses material space and the Gauntlet in Earth doesn't cross that space. If the &quot;joint&quot; of both beyond the Horizon impedes to see Umbrood past that point then the sepparation exists in some form or another (either there's a Gauntlet sepparating the Deep Umbra from the Deep Space that's paralel to our own and clearly divides spirit from matter - and then the realms aren't intermingled -, or there's a Gauntlet that bubbles us in the Asteroid Belt, which seems to be what the VE Convention book says with the Lensing effect starting there). And if the separation impedes my sight then it should also impede traveling there by Correspondence because we're talking about a spiritual barrier here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-19-2018, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T09:56:50-07:00","id":1261597,"title":"","content":"Hmm. How's this work for a frame? I think it's all defensible given the cosmology information we have, though obviously others may differ.<br /> <br /> Think of the various worlds as colors of light. They're stacked/intermingled, but the Gauntlet separates them out into three Umbrae and one material realm.<br /> <br /> The Gauntlet ensures that the material world - red light - is separated from the other colors.<br /> <br /> The Horizon is where the light unites (or, going the other way, separates). Beyond it, it's all white light, for the purpose of this metaphor.<br /> <br /> (Umbral stargazers see the Umbral heavens. Possibly three different flavors of them, in fact - the Aetherial Realms vs. the Shard Realms, for instance.)<br /> <br /> I think that Tegmark lensing wasn't necessary to explain why Sleepers don't see umbral events, because - using the metaphor - material reality only perceives material space, the space illuminated by red light. Material probes travel through red-space, and the Anthropic Horizon reflects spaces where the Gauntlet has been pushed outwards, splitting the white light.<br /> <br /> That is, that the Anthropic Horizon doesn't create more red light/material space, but creates a larger volume of space where the material and spiritual are separated.<br /> <br /> If you were in the Anthropic Horizon, your telescope would still see only material reality, because there's a Gauntlet. You can also reach this place physically, which is indeed how the various space probes got there. Correspondence could probably teleport you there.<br /> <br /> If you had crossed the Horizon with DimSci, your telescope would see everything, and if you turned it back towards Earth, you'd see both material Earth and the three Umbral Earths, stacked on top of eachother, because you're in a place where the colors of light aren't differentiated.<br /> <br /> As you returned back into the inner solar system and passed back through the Horizon, you'd be sorted into one of the various otherworlds, and your observation of Earth would be limited accordingly.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T10:56:46-07:00","id":1261616,"title":"","content":"I think I understand better now, but I don't think it solves the problem:<br /> <br /> If the red stream really unites with the others at some point then a particle traveling trough the red stream up to that point should be able to cross with particles traveling trough the others. If you need magick to do that passage and interact with other streams, then they aren't really intermingled. Or at least not more intermingled than in Earth, anyway. And if you can travel physically to that point then your physical sight should be able to do the same.<br /> <br /> If I were to travel in a mundane rocket past the volume of space where the material and spiritual are separated, and I still can't see or interact with other than &quot;red light entities&quot; without Spirit magic, how it's that different from a Gauntlet sepparating spirit from matter?.\u200b And if I can interact with the other beams at that point, then why my eyes were impaired to do so a moment ago?.<br /> <br /> Theres a canon example of intermingled realms interacting with humans: Shalowings. Humans in a Shalowing can see spirits, they can see everything.<br /> <br /> Personally I think your idea (as I understand it) it's the better way to do this - a &quot;soft&quot; sepparation between the realms that's very weak, yet allows one to travel to another planet without mixing with the Umbra if one desires so - but I don't think that's what VE: Convention Book authors were aiming at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-19-2018, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T11:21:34-07:00","id":1261622,"title":"","content":"I don't follow you on this part:<br /> <br /> <b>If I were to travel in a mundane rocket past the volume of space where the material and spiritual are separated, and I still can't see or interact with other than &quot;red light entities&quot; without Spirit magic, how it's that different from a Gauntlet separating spirit from matter?</b><br /> <br /> You <i>can </i>physically travel into the material stream of the outer solar system - it's what Sleeper space probes do, and it created the Anthropic Horizon, which is material outer space with a Gauntlet. It should also be possible to Correspondence yourself to, say, Anthropic Jupiter, because it's in physical space and it's differentiated from other layers by a Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> A Sleeper brought (using Spirit/DimSci) into the Deep Umbra would see everything just as they would in a Shallowing, where colors of light intermingle.<br /> <br /> (What's uncertain is if mages can use Spirit 3 to cross from Anthropic Horizon into the Umbral version of a planet. Werewolves can Step Sideways in this way, but it would mean you could use Corr + Spirit to arrive somewhere in the Deep Umbra that normally requires Spirit Mastery to reach.)<br /> <br /> It's apparently not possible to Correspond to material Pluto (past the Anthropic Horizon), presumably because your destination is entangled with Umbral realities in such a way as to be beyond Correspondence alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T13:15:02-07:00","id":1261636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261460#post1261460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the World of Darkness isn't our world. And the vast majority of people in the World of Darkness are ignorant Sheeple who really are that stupid that a handful of Order of Reason Mages can reshape the entire planet without anyone noticing any different one discovery at a time. Because that's the attitude the counterculture loving hippies at White Wolf had about the vast majority of people. That there are a few 'enlightened' who know what 'The Man' is up to, but most are just braindead idiots.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be a running theme, but I've never seen it explicitly stated anywhere. So I willfully choose to ignore that bit of rather unflattering context. Not much of an argument maybe, but I'll stick with it.<br /> <br /> Besides, I think making the masses ignorant sheeple seems kinda runs counter to one of WoD themes of not making the PCs much more special than the average joe(Beyond being forced to confront the supernatural one day). It makes it unlike most RPGs where the PCs are treated like Messiah figures destined to save the world/destroy it in setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T14:11:04-07:00","id":1261641,"title":"","content":"First a few things. Just read page 55-56 of the VE book:<br /> <br /> Jupiter it's within the <b>Deep Universe</b>, a region marked past the Asteroid belt, while the Antrophic Horizon only extends over &quot;<i>some regions</i>&quot; of that area, as per the map you mentioned on page 55.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Book</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond the Spatial Horizon lies the <b>Deep Universe</b>, a realm that lacks even the physical laws unEnlightened citizens believe exist. Far from the Masses\u2019 Anthropic Principle, humans require advanced Dimensional Science to survive. No Dimensional Gauntlet separates regions in the true Void.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Book</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Deep Universe</b>: Travelers must travel across Conventional Space or Subspace to the Spatial Horizon <b>and then employ Dimensional Science 5</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Note how it mentions <b>the Deep Universe</b>,<i> the space that's marked just past the Asteroid Belt minus &quot;some regions&quot;</i>. And not <i>Interestellar Deep</i> that's past Pluto.See how the division between matter and spirit isn't marked in the Deep Universe (or rather, it is, but in a small rectangle rather than encompassing the area), that's important.<br /> <br /> It's important that they decided to mark the separation between spirit and matter in all the space covered by the inner solar system, but only made two small squares to represent that in the outer solar system. It's ijmportant that they decided to signal the start of the Deep Universe (that section where you need Mastery of Spirit to travel) at the Asteroid Belt. <i>It really seems to me like they intended Deep Universe to refer to the outer solar system</i>, with the &quot;some places&quot; mentioned in the Antrophic Horizon being the exception to the rule.<br /> <br /> Aesthetically, the Gauntlet it's WAY less marked over that region. Linguistically the &quot;some regions&quot; isn't specific but certainly isn't superlative, much less all-encompassing. One would need to torture that map a lot to make it say that the outer solar system isn't mostly part of the Deep Universe. Not reachable by Correspondence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> =Five Eyes I don't follow you on this part:<br /> <br /> <b>If I were to travel in a mundane rocket past the volume of space where the material and spiritual are separated, and I still can't see or interact with other than &quot;red light entities&quot; without Spirit magic, how it's that different from a Gauntlet separating spirit from matter?</b><br /> <br /> You <i>can </i>physically travel into the material stream of the outer solar system - it's what Sleeper space probes do, and it created the Anthropic Horizon, which is material outer space with a Gauntlet. It should also be possible to Correspondence yourself to, say, because it's in physical space and it's differentiated from other layers by a Gauntlet. </div> </div> </div>Let's go way back to the begining:<br /> <br /> Premise 1: Material Outer Space it's infinite, extending beyond the Horizons, and there doesn't need to be no Tegmar Lensing.<br /> <br /> Rigth?. The whole premise was that an astronomer watching Alpha Centauri it's watching material Alpha Centauri<br /> <br /> Premise 2: Past the Asteroid Belts (and very few specific places like the moons of Jupiter) there isn't a Gauntlet sepparating matter from spirit.<br /> <br /> This is a consesion to VE: Convention Book<br /> <br /> NOW, I'm trying to point that in your example sight and travel work fundamentally different, in such a way that it's not compatible with your premises:<br /> <br /> My sight can see red light past the Anthropic Horizon. It has to if I'm supposed to watch material Alpha Centauri without the oddities of the Umbra, without a Gauntlet sepparating spirit from matter, and without a Tegmark Lensing.<br /> <br /> Yet it seems that to travel physically there first I need to &quot;create an Anthropic Horizon&quot; complete with a Gauntlet (something only unEnligthened people and probes can do without further magick), expanding the area of red light.<br /> <br /> Travel and sight don't match. The problem it's that for sight to see only red light and no white light beyond the point where my rocked created a Gauntlet there needs to be some sort of &quot;gauntlet-esque&quot; thing &quot;covering&quot; the other colors of light, much like in Earth. Either that or I'm seeing an illusion, because the Gauntlet isn't there yet, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T14:53:38-07:00","id":1261647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261641#post1261641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet it seems that to travel physically there first I need to &quot;create an Anthropic Horizon&quot; complete with a Gauntlet (something only unEnligthened people and probes can do without further magick), expanding the area of red light.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's backwards, though - it was by traveling there physicallythat the Anthropic Horizon was created. The oddity is that mages seem incapable of undertaking the same journey with Correspondence, though they may be able to get there the slow way using Sleeper methods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261641#post1261641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The problem it's that for sight to see only red light and no white light beyond the point where my rocket created a Gauntlet there needs to be some sort of &quot;gauntlet-esque&quot; thing &quot;covering&quot; the other colors of light, much like in Earth. Either that or I'm seeing an illusion, because the Gauntlet isn't there yet, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> If only red light passes through the Gauntlet, it doesn't matter how many colors of light Deep Umbral Neptune is giving off - an observer that's on Earth (or in a material rocket within the Anthropic Horizon) is only going to see the red.<br /> <br /> Nothing needs to be happening to, or wrapped around, <i>the flowers </i>for my colorblindness to affect what <i>I </i>see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":".  Capable and incapable mean different things. 10-20-2018, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T17:36:23-07:00","id":1261674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261647#post1261647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's backwards, though - it was by traveling there physicallythat the Anthropic Horizon was created. The oddity is that mages seem capable of undertaking the same journey with Correspondence, though they may be able to get there the slow way using Sleeper methods.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>They can't undertake the <i>same </i>journey with Correspondence.</b> As per the pages I quoted before, the Deep Universe can't be reached by Correspondence alone. Unless that space was already formated (i.e. Part of Conventional Space, what you call &quot;whitin the Antrophic Horizon&quot; - as can be seen in p.55, where they describe each area of the Umbra) you can't get there by Correspondence. Hence you need to, as I said: &quot;create an Anthropic Horizon&quot; (Conventional Space) complete with a Gauntlet (something only unEnligthened people and probes can do without further magick), expanding the area of red light, to get there physically with Correspondence.<br /> <br /> Mundane travel expands the bubble, but that something expands the bubble doesn't prove that the bubble doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why?<br /> <br /> If only red light passes through the Gauntlet, it doesn't matter how many colors of light Deep Umbral Neptune is giving off - an observer that's on Earth (or in a material rocket within the Anthropic Horizon) is only going to see the red.<br /> <br /> Nothing needs to be happening to, or wrapped around, <i>the flowers </i>for my colorblindness to affect what <i>I </i>see. </div> </div> </div>In Earth a flower may have a spiritual side. RAW you don't see it because there's a Gauntlet that sepparates spirit from matter. That's the very definition of The Gauntlet, a barrier between Realms. You're comparing this with being color blind in your example, right?.<br /> <br /> As far as I know there's nothing that impedes to see a spirit inside a Shalowing from outside the Shalowing, as long as there's a clear path between you and the Shalowing you're not &quot;color blind&quot;. Nothing I've heard says that a sleeper can't see inside a Spirit 4 Portal that conects to the Umbra regardless of the fact that they're still in a place with a Gauntlet before entering said Portal. In other words, being whitin a place that has a Gauntlet does not impede to see trough a place that has no Gauntlet<br /> <br /> Thus, if you're saying that the same phenomena aplies to the many colors of light Deep Umbral Neptune is giving off, you're saying that there's a Gauntlet sepparating stuff between the observer and the object.<br /> <br /> Then you're implying that such Gauntlet exists, and it's like some sort of red crystal ceiling that only allows red beams to pass, distorting our view. I'm following you?<br /> <br /> <i>That's undistinguishable from the Tegmark Lensing Effect</i>. It effectively means that outer space as we understand it doesn't exist because there's a barrier (the barrier that separates the Umbra from Physical Realm) between my telescope and said outer space that prevents me from seeing stuff right. I'm receiving distorted data that conveniently rips off all that spiritual nastyness that the Consensus doesn't like.<br /> <br /> One might even dare to say that such barrier has to exist somewhere arround the Asteroid Belt, because being whitin a place that has a Gauntlet does not impede to see trough a place that's not surrounded by a Gauntlet, and after that point there's no Gauntlet<br /> <br /> The only difference from that and saying outer space it's the Umbra it's that, perhaps, Matter Sphere isn't useless past that border. And not much more, really. Humans still disembody if they stay there too long, most aliens are still spirits 'cause we don't see them, and outer space it's still a crazy place that doesn't obey the rules of science and astronomers doesn't know because they're color-blinded by the red curtain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-19-2018, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-19T18:29:58-07:00","id":1261682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261674#post1261674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Hence you need to, as I said: &quot;create an Anthropic Horizon&quot; (Conventional Space) complete with a Gauntlet (something only unEnligthened people and probes can do without further magick), expanding the area of red light, to get there physically with Correspondence.<br /> <br /> Mundane travel expands the bubble, but that something expands the bubble doesn't prove that the bubble doesn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's no red light beyond the asteroid belt - if materiality ends there - what are mundane travelers traveling <i>into?</i><br /> <br /> Why would we assume that &quot;Realspace and etherspace become indistinguishable&quot; actually means &quot;there is no realspace beyond this point&quot; - that'd be a very peculiar reading, wouldn't it? My contention is that I think it's more accurate to say that, for those in the Deep Umbra, the various colors are intermingled, and that the expansion of the Gauntlet splits them back out. It doesn't make more red light than already existed, it just divides the realities, just as the otherworlds are typically divided on Earth. This is why, for example, CB:VE can say things like &quot;Conventional Jupiter&quot; - we understand that this means Earthrealm Jupiter, even though the celestial body is beyond the Spatial Horizon.<br /> <br /> This means that space beyond the Spatial Horizon isn't &quot;the umbra&quot;; it's a place where the three umbrae and materiality intermingle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261674#post1261674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you're implying that such Gauntlet exists, and it's like some sort of red crystal ceiling that only allows red beams to pass, distorting our view. I'm following you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Close - I think that being in a divided (Gauntlet-bounded, etc.) part of a Realm would be sufficient to explain why we don't see Deep Umbral events in their full spectrum. That's why I feel like Tegmark lensing as an idea is unnecessary - we don't need the Spatial Horizon to have an effect on perceptions to make Earthrealm eyes only see Earthrealm stuff. But, as you pointed out, it doesn't jibe with what happens when you breach the Gauntlet on earth - on reflection, I'm inclined to gloss that over, because I think it's tidier (and fits Mage's themes better) than having a layer of occult deception on the asteroid belt.<br /> <br /> I'm likening being in the divided parts of Earthrealm as akin to being in a red crystal bubble; the Anthropic Horizon makes the bubble larger, but Conventional Space isn't all of materiality - just the part within the red crystal filter. There's red light outside of our bubble (which we can see), among the other colors (which we cannot.)<br /> <br /> That's why I compared it to looking at the night sky from the bottom of a well - there's no wall in the stars that's making us see things incompletely, it's the result of the viewer's perspective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261674#post1261674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It effectively means that outer space as we understand it doesn't exist because there's a barrier (the barrier that separates the Umbra from Physical Realm) between my telescope and said outer space that prevents me from seeing stuff right. I'm receiving distorted data that conveniently rips off all that spiritual nastyness that the Consensus doesn't like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely it &quot;doesn't exist&quot; in the same way that stuff on Earth &quot;doesn't exist&quot; - your binoculars and microscopes aren't showing you the Umbral layers of terrestrial reality, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-20T13:32:05-07:00","id":1261822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261682#post1261682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there's no red light beyond the asteroid belt - if materiality ends there - what are mundane travelers traveling <i>into?</i><br /> <br /> Why would we assume that &quot;Realspace and etherspace become indistinguishable&quot; actually means &quot;there is no realspace beyond this point&quot; - that'd be a very peculiar reading, wouldn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The book implies that they travel &quot;into&quot; the space they previously Format with their perception, like a drill carving into stone. And you don't Format realspace, you Format the Umbra. That's why the way mages do that very thing uses Spirit 5. That's why you can't Correspond to space that hasn't been Formated yet from the material space unless you use Spirit.<br /> <br /> What I'm reading to say that &quot;there is no realspace beyond this point&quot; it's that beyond that point space looses all it's properties, them being replaced by all the properties of the Umbra. Beyond that point you need Spirit to travel, the body turns into spirit after three moons, and the inhabitants are Umbrood.<br /> <br /> If it looks like a duck, sounds like a duck, and acts like a duck...<br /> <br /> If by materiality you mean stuff that's passible of being affected by the Matter Sphere, then sure it doesn't end at the Gauntlet. If nothing else Hollow Earth proves it doesn't. But's that's not what I mean when I say materiality. To say that the elements that comprise outer space are present in the Deep Umbra it's just not enough .I don't care if there's real dust at the other side of the Gauntlet if it's still a world of spirit that one needs Spirit magick to reach, where dematerialization it's the norm and Umbrood it's inhabitants, then I can't use it the way I would use realspace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My contention is that I think it's more accurate to say that, for those in the Deep Umbra, the various colors are intermingled, and that the expansion of the Gauntlet splits them back out. It doesn't make more red light than already existed, it just divides the realities, just as the otherworlds are typically divided on Earth. This is why, for example, CB:VE can say things like &quot;Conventional Jupiter&quot; - we understand that this means Earthrealm Jupiter, even though the celestial body is beyond the Spatial Horizon. </div> </div> </div>Where do they talk about that?<br /> <br /> I ask because not all Jupiter is beyond the Spatial Horizon, remember that probes expand the Spatial Horizon, that's what the weird squares in the Deep Space zone mean. I'm 100% certain that the moons of Jupiter are fully whitin the Spatial Horizon, and they have a realspace and etherspace. I'm not so sure about the rest of Jupiter, much less the rest of the solar system, but the squares do extend up to Saturn, and thus it's possible that they were refering to parts of Jupiter that were already formatted, rather than about a &quot;non Deep Space Jupiter&quot; that needs to be discovered, can be traveled w/o Spirit and it's material and all.<br /> <br /> If they do use the word Conventional for places that are beyond the Antrophic Horizon I may reconsider my point, but precisely Jupiter it's the platet that's more likely to be whitin the expanded areas of that Horizon<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Surely it &quot;doesn't exist&quot; in the same way that stuff on Earth &quot;doesn't exist&quot; - your binoculars and microscopes aren't showing you the Umbral layers of terrestrial reality, either. </div> </div> </div>Of course, that's what I'm saying. Spiritual stuff on Earth doesn't exist: It's in the Umbra. They're sepparate.<br /> <br /> And precisely because they're sepparated Umbral rules don't eat Eartly rules and viceversa (for instance: Bygones don't need to be Umbrood). Personally, I would rather have it be the same with outer space stuff. That way astronomers don't get the complete picture and outer space is not the Umbra at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-20-2018, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-20T15:58:22-07:00","id":1261848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261822#post1261822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book implies that they travel &quot;into&quot; the space they previously Format with their perception, like a drill carving into stone. And you don't Format realspace, you Format the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like an inelegant interpretation of what's happening. The Anthropic Horizon is being pushed back by unmanned probes - the tools of perception itself - so if perception is creating the space that is being perceived to create the space into which the probe travels to make further observations... what's it perceiving?<br /> <br /> Would it also fit to evidence to say that the Anthropic Horizon is an extension of the thickening of the terrestrial Gauntlet under scientific observation, which is done in Realspace?<br /> <br /> Does Tegmark lensing create an illusion, or does it do what CB:VE says it does - <i>censor </i>what is perceived?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261822#post1261822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why the way mages do that very thing uses Spirit 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Format Space actually doesn'tuse Spirit 5. It uses Correspondence 5, DimSci 4 - the spheres you'd use to overlap a region with the corresponding space of a coterminous Realm. This is probably meant to be an extension of DimSci 4's Stabilize Dimensional Field, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261822#post1261822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do they talk about that? I ask because not all Jupiter is beyond the Spatial Horizon...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was looking at the section on Shard Realms in CB:VE (Starts on pg 63); Mage is usually pretty clear that the physical planets anchor the Shards, and Infinite Tapestry talks about physical space as distinct from Umbral, so I figured that the Shard Realm section would be where to look for any echoes of the BoW-style notes on the properties of &quot;material&quot; versions of the various planets.<br /> <br /> I agree that Jupiter is close enough to have some Conventional reaches, but I still feel as though the interpretation that the outer planets don't really exist is paddling against the way that BoW and M20 talk about Realspace and Etherspace intermingling and how we know the various Realms tend to &quot;stack&quot; on the same anchor point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261822#post1261822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And precisely because they're separated Umbral rules don't eat Eartly rules and viceversa (for instance: Bygones don't need to be Umbrood). Personally, I would rather have it be the same with outer space stuff. That way astronomers don't get the complete picture and outer space is not the Umbra at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I follow you - you're saying that it's not meaningful if Realspace is intertwined with Etherspace, because that means that the drawbacks and hazards of Otherworldly travel occur as if you were in Etherspace (which, after all, you are), right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T12:12:23-07:00","id":1261965,"title":"","content":"I would suggest that what you've been calling a \u201cred filter\u201d that causes Sleepers to only see those aspects of the Deep Universe that correspond to \u201cEarthspace\u201d is, in fact, what CBVE is talking about when it mentions \u201cTegmark Lensing\u201d: despite the phrasing, it doesn't cause illusions of things that aren't out there; rather, it blinds the viewer to those aspects that don't match what you'd expect to find in Conventional Space. This isn't the same as Conventional Space extending outward indefinitely, because Correspondence still stops at the Spatial Horizon and things on the other side of said Horizon are still cut off from Earth's Primal Energy and thus subject to Void Adaptation. <br /> <br /> Now, CBVE clearly indicates that unmanned space probes are enough to create tendrils of Conventional Space beyond the Spatial Horizon. <i>This</i> is the bit that <i>I</i> take issue with, especially with M20's institution of Reality Zones: per my understanding of the Consensus, it simply shouldn't have the reach to enable an unmanned probe to Format Space. I could possibly see a <i>manned</i> spacecraft with a sufficiently large crew (think \u201ccolony ship\u201d, with hundreds or thousands of people on board) effectively surrounding itself in a bubble of Conventional Space as it penetrates the Spatial Horizon and voyages into the Deep Universe; but I don't see a ship with a crew of a dozen or less, let alone an unmanned probe, managing this. <br /> <br /> So why haven't our space probes run into the Spatial Horizon and revealed its existence to the world at large? In my head-canon, it's because the Void Engineers shepherd the space probes, guiding then through the Spatial Horizon and protecting them from the threats of the Deep Universe; because humanity can't be allowed to know what's out there. Tegmark Lensing helps with this, as the space probes' signals get filtered as they cross the Spatial Horizon on their way back to Earth; but that is not, in and of itself, enough to protect the secret. Active measures by Enlightened personnel are needed to preserve it. <br /> <br /> But again, that's my head-canon. As far as I know, M20 hasn't addressed the issue of space probes entering the Deep Universe; only CBVE has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T12:45:34-07:00","id":1261970,"title":"","content":"Let me ask this, what would be the downside if I just said there is a material space, but it has a low gauntlet? What am I loosing? You can even include other worlds as right on the other side of the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Like what if the penumbra of spaces isn\u2019t like the normal penumbra but is always the near or deep Umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T13:38:09-07:00","id":1261982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261965#post1261965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest that what you've been calling a \u201cred filter\u201d that causes Sleepers to only see those aspects of the Deep Universe that correspond to \u201cEarthspace\u201d is, in fact, what CBVE is talking about when it mentions \u201cTegmark Lensing\u201d: despite the phrasing, it doesn't cause illusions of things that aren't out there; rather, it blinds the viewer to those aspects that don't match what you'd expect to find in Conventional Space. This isn't the same as Conventional Space extending outward indefinitely, because Correspondence still stops at the Spatial Horizon and things on the other side of said Horizon are still cut off from Earth's Primal Energy and thus subject to Void Adaptation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this is what Tegmark lensing is doing; I feel as though we didn't strictly need a new thing to describe something that the Gauntlet already does: prevent material eyes from seeing immaterial events.<br /> <br /> I also concur that Conventional Space (Realspace + Gauntlet) doesn't continue indefinitely, but I suspect that Realspace <i>does</i> - that the material space that the Anthropic Horizon is extended into already exists (normally, intermingling with Etherspace), and that the Anthropic Horizon is an extension of the Gauntlet, instead of the extension of Realspace. In my first post, I got the two muddled, and was using &quot;conventional space&quot; to mean &quot;material space as we readers understand it&quot;, not as the proper term capital-C-Conventional. (I'm pretty sure you've corrected me on that before, so I apologize.)<br /> <br /> Tidily, thickening a Gauntlet with scientific observation is easier than creating a Reality Zone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1261970#post1261970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me ask this, what would be the downside if I just said there is a material space, but it has a low gauntlet? What am I loosing? You can even include other worlds as right on the other side of the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Like what if the penumbra of spaces isn\u2019t like the normal penumbra but is always the near or deep Umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much changes; the Deep Umbra is already sort of layered. Strictly speaking this makes Deep Umbral travel easier (if you can Corr 3/Spirit 3 to the Deep Umbra) or harder (if you think this means you can't use Spirit alone to travel there.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T16:42:33-07:00","id":1262017,"title":"","content":"Conventional Space and Realspace are the same thing. It's not the presence of absence of the Gauntlet that matters; it's the presence or absence of Umbrood and, for lack of a better term, Umbral physics. In Conventional Space, you don't have to worry about Void Adaptation, and you <i>do</i> have to worry about Vulgar Magick. On the other side of the Gauntlet, or on the other side of the Spatial Horizon (which amounts to the same thing), you <i>do</i> have to worry about Void Adaptation, and you generally <i>don't</i> have to worry about Paradox. As well, you can't just fly past the Spatial Horizon: it's a <i>barrier to travel</i> that either requires Spirit/Dimensional Science or the full weight of the Consensus backing you up to cross (and the latter isn't so much a case of crossing it as it is pushing it back, which really shouldn't be easy to do). The biggest difference between the Gauntlet and the Spatial Horizon in this regard is that crossing the Gauntlet is described as \u201cStepping Sideways\u201d, where your three-dimensional position doesn't change but you move to a parallel layer of reality; crossing the Spatial Horizon is more a matter of \u201cstepping <i>forward</i>\u201d: you don't shift to another layer, but instead move outward from the Sun across the literal edge of space into the Void that lies beyond it. It's the fact that you have to leave regular space when you cross the Horizon that is why you can't use Correspondence to cross it. <br /> <br /> The biggest drawback of saying that normal space extends indefinitely is that it lets the Void Engineers set up bases on deep space that would have no problem coping with things like the Avatar Storm; their only problems would involve maintaining supplies and keeping their technology running while travel to and from Earth is hazardous (which can be a challenge, but is nothing compared to the near certainty of Void Adaptation mere months after being cut off from Earth). And even that's not much of an issue if you have some teleporters in place: without the Spatial Horizon acting as a barrier to travel, there's nothing preventing them from just building a Stargate-like network to keep their far-flung colonies connected without risking any of the dangers of the Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T17:19:56-07:00","id":1262022,"title":"","content":"I disagree with that interpretation.<br /> <br /> Both Book of Worlds (pg 148) and M20 (pg 114) say that Realspace and Etherspace become difficult to distinguish in the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> If Realspace ends where the Deep Umbra begins, they would be <i>extremely easy </i>to distinguish.<br /> <br /> I don't think this means that you can Correspond to Neptune, but rather that material reality is one of the intertwined &quot;layers&quot; that make up the Deep Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T19:08:06-07:00","id":1262033,"title":"","content":"My point is that if it were a layer, <i>that</i> would be easy to distinguish from Etherspace. They're \u201chard to distinguish\u201d because they're <i>not</i> layered; they're blended into something that's neither Etherspace nor \u201cRealspace\u201d, as you call it \u2014 though functionally the result is much more like Etherspace than \u201cRealspace\u201d, with the main \u201cRealspace\u201d contribution probably being its hostility to life. <br /> <br /> And again, it's not just that you can't teleport across the boundary; you can't <i>fly</i> across it either. The transition from Realspace to the Void is something that requires something akin to the ability to Step Sideways to manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T20:32:23-07:00","id":1262042,"title":"","content":"I can't look at a white light and only see the red parts, but it's still made of multiple wavelengths. A prism - a Gauntlet, or Formatting - can split it out.<br /> <br /> And the Anthropic Horizon exists because something <i>was</i> flown across that impassible boundary. Or, at least, across its material component. Do we think a manned Sleepertech vessel would bounce off if a mage was sitting inside it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T21:16:42-07:00","id":1262047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1262022#post1262022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with that interpretation.<br /> <br /> Both Book of Worlds (pg 148) and M20 (pg 114) say that Realspace and Etherspace become difficult to distinguish in the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> If Realspace ends where the Deep Umbra begins, they would be <i>extremely easy </i>to distinguish.<br /> <br /> I don't think this means that you can Correspond to Neptune, but rather that material reality is one of the intertwined &amp;quot;layers&amp;quot; that make up the Deep Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>See this is what I can get behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T21:19:12-07:00","id":1262048,"title":"","content":"At what point can you teleport though? I mean if you had a good enough rocket can\u2019t you go there? Only if it\u2019s going into the deep Umbra do you need a membrane to cross but if rockets can go there maybe you can use corresponded to get there but only if you are already near.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T00:04:20-07:00","id":1262074,"title":"","content":"I agree that the notion that a Sleeper machine can just sail on through when a mage gets blocked is ridiculous. But there's a lot more evidence that the mage gets blocked than that the Sleeper machine gets through: the latter is something only mentioned in CBVE, and even then only in passing (three mentions in the entire book, and two of them are compatible with the notion that those space probes are VE tools); the former is mentioned in Book of Worlds, Infinite Tapestry, CBVE, and M20, each time in the form of explicit rules about what you need to cross the Spatial Horizon. So my inclination is to say that CBVE is wrong about Sleeper probes being able to extend Conventional Space into the Deep Universe unassisted; thus my speculation that the ones that got through had help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-22-2018, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T06:26:08-07:00","id":1262837,"title":"","content":"What if I have just a very thin Gauntlet in the Void, and like mentioned by someone earlier I go with the notion Mages are natural shallowings so when encountering weak Gauntlets they are pushed through. But what if away from Earth the Materialize capability is rarer, or even maybe spirits aren\u2019t aware they can do it being so far away from Earth.<br /> <br /> Perhaps without the stabilizing effects of the pilopulation of Earth instead of no material space what we actually have is just no Penumbra for space, just the layers Mages know of, and the Aetherial Realm of the Garou?<br /> <br /> Also one of the Big implications of the World of Darkness is the unmapped terrain is Faeryland. The Faeholdings from the Dark Ages were the wild unmapped Secret portions of the world, and eventually they were pushed into the Dreaming when that formed and became its own thing. The Freeholds were the tinier stabler bits of Faeryland, while ancient Holdings became whole subrealms. This leads me to believe space could be heavily linked to the Dreaming. The Deep Dreaming and Deep Umbra always seemed two sides of the same coin to me, just perceived differently.<br /> <br /> So are the natural Denizens of Space maybe either Fae and or Umbrood? So Inanimae that come from Meteors, are they truly old or always new? Are Space Fae just Fae that never met with earthly Dreams?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T02:19:26-07:00","id":1263036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1262837#post1262837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if I have just a very thin Gauntlet in the Void, and like mentioned by someone earlier I go with the notion Mages are natural shallowings so when encountering weak Gauntlets they are pushed through. But what if away from Earth the Materialize capability is rarer, or even maybe spirits aren\u2019t aware they can do it being so far away from Earth.<br /> <br /> Perhaps without the stabilizing effects of the pilopulation of Earth instead of no material space what we actually have is just no Penumbra for space, just the layers Mages know of, and the Aetherial Realm of the Garou?<br /> <br /> Also one of the Big implications of the World of Darkness is the unmapped terrain is Faeryland. The Faeholdings from the Dark Ages were the wild unmapped Secret portions of the world, and eventually they were pushed into the Dreaming when that formed and became its own thing. The Freeholds were the tinier stabler bits of Faeryland, while ancient Holdings became whole subrealms. This leads me to believe space could be heavily linked to the Dreaming. The Deep Dreaming and Deep Umbra always seemed two sides of the same coin to me, just perceived differently.<br /> <br /> So are the natural Denizens of Space maybe either Fae and or Umbrood? So Inanimae that come from Meteors, are they truly old or always new? Are Space Fae just Fae that never met with earthly Dreams?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In some book a character made a notion about the Dreaming being the Umbra of the moon, rather than Earth and Moon being the shard realm of Prime. They discussed this quite briefly and without any real evidence, but it could explain the similarities of Deep Dreaming and Deep Umbra as both exist very far from their respective anchor, actually bleeding into each other and becoming one thing.<br /> I believe it was the Book of Worlds, but I'd have to go through my library to make sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T09:50:55-07:00","id":1263076,"title":"","content":"That is definitely a popular theory I hear around a the Bend. To help explain the Moonlanding opening the Gates of Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T16:48:52-07:00","id":1263145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1262837#post1262837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if I have just a very thin Gauntlet in the Void, and like mentioned by someone earlier I go with the notion Mages are natural shallowings so when encountering weak Gauntlets they are pushed through. But what if away from Earth the Materialize capability is rarer, or even maybe spirits aren\u2019t aware they can do it being so far away from Earth.<br /> <br /> Perhaps without the stabilizing effects of the pilopulation of Earth instead of no material space what we actually have is just no Penumbra for space, just the layers Mages know of, and the Aetherial Realm of the Garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're free to do it however you want, of course. But the above would not be consistent with published material, for a few reasons: first, there are no indications of anything that <i>doesn't</i> \u201cfall through\u201d: not mages, not spirits, not Sleepers. Heck, Void Engineers, who practice a Dimensional Science where the effective strength of the Gauntlet differs from the Traditional Spirit magick and who have a Focus most favorable to Conventional Space extending outward indefinitely, are the ones who would be <i>least</i> likely to \u201cfall through\u201d a thin Gauntlet into a separate Void. But <i>even they</i> \u201cfall through\u201d. (By which I mean, once they cross the Spatial Horizon into the Deep Universe, they find themselves in \u201cunformatted space\u201d, i.e. something that's a heck of a lot more like the Umbra than it is like the material world.) Put another way: if <i>everything</i> falls through the \u201cweak Gauntlet\u201d that you're suggesting extends even into the Deep Umbra, how is that different from there <i>not being a Gauntlet at all,</i> out there?<br /> <br /> As well, that doesn't address the Spatial Horizon, which <i>prevents mages from entering the Deep Universe.</i> If you can just fly to Neptune without needing Spirit 5 to cross the Horizon, it would be pretty darn easy to distinguish between regular space and the Umbra; and conversely, if a mage who gets past the Spatial Horizon using \u201cEarthspace\u201d automatically \u201cfalls through\u201d an ultra-thin Gauntlet into the Umbra, that would be a <i>massive</i> loophole that would render utterly moot the need for Spirit 5 to enter the Deep Universe. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1262837#post1262837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also one of the Big implications of the World of Darkness is the unmapped terrain is Faeryland. The Faeholdings from the Dark Ages were the wild unmapped Secret portions of the world, and eventually they were pushed into the Dreaming when that formed and became its own thing. The Freeholds were the tinier stabler bits of Faeryland, while ancient Holdings became whole subrealms. This leads me to believe space could be heavily linked to the Dreaming. The Deep Dreaming and Deep Umbra always seemed two sides of the same coin to me, just perceived differently.<br /> <br /> So are the natural Denizens of Space maybe either Fae and or Umbrood? So Inanimae that come from Meteors, are they truly old or always new? Are Space Fae just Fae that never met with earthly Dreams?</div> </div> </div> </div>Various Umbra-related supplements indicate that the Dreaming is what is called a \u201cZone\u201d: that is, it's separate from the Umbra, just like the Digital Web site separate from the Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T16:57:22-07:00","id":1263146,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not saying everything falls, but Mages unconsciously fall, everything else goes into space like normal. And it doesn\u2019t make it unnecessary, after all spacecraft are normally billions of dollars, but perhaps they need it, but other means don\u2019t need it and can travel like normal. Or maybe they are in a dangerous void if they don\u2019t use it, like the Abyss.<br /> <br /> What happens if a mage goes on a Normal Nasa rocket? They don\u2019t need to cast spells yet wouldn\u2019t they be going into space?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T17:14:52-07:00","id":1263147,"title":"","content":"And also don\u2019t most Technocrats travel to space while already in the Umbra. What examples do we have of them just going on a material rocket?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T20:05:23-07:00","id":1263154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1263146#post1263146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not saying everything falls, but Mages unconsciously fall, everything else goes into space like normal. And it doesn\u2019t make it unnecessary, after all spacecraft are normally billions of dollars, but perhaps they need it, but other means don\u2019t need it and can travel like normal. Or maybe they are in a dangerous void if they don\u2019t use it, like the Abyss.<br /> <br /> What happens if a mage goes on a Normal Nasa rocket? They don\u2019t need to cast spells yet wouldn\u2019t they be going into space?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <i>you're</i> not assuming that everything \u201cfalls through\u201d; <i>I'm</i> saying that there's no evidence of anything <i>not</i> \u201cfalling through\u201d, save for literally three off-hand comments in CBVE which <i>could</i> be interpreted as space probes extending Conventional Space (a feat that normally requires mastery of both Dimensional Science and Void Correspondence and a lot of deliberate effort, and which is supposedly being done millions of miles away from the nearest human being, spontaneously, just by a hunk of metal drifting through space), or could be interpreted as instruments in an ongoing Void Engineer Procedure to Format the Deep Universe. <br /> <br /> And it's that question of \u201cwhat happens if a mage goes on a normal NASA rocket?\u201d which was the <i>whole point</i> of my talk about the Spatial Horizon: if regular space extends beyond the Spatial Horizon and you don't need magick to penetrate it, then by your theory, as soon as you cross the Spatial Horizon, the mage \u201cfalls through\u201d into the Deep Umbra. Whee; that was easy! (Yes, getting to the Horizon in normal space has its own challenges; but they're minor compared to needing Spirit 5; a simple teleport spell from Earth to a space probe would do the trick. And comparatively minor Matter and Forces magicks could help build a spacecraft and propel it to the Spatial Horizon \u2014 and, according to your theory, beyond. Heck, why not use Subspace to get to the Horizon, then drop out of Subspace in order to \u201cduck under\u201d the Spatial Barrier? Either Spirit 5 to cross from Subspace into the Deep Universe, or Spirit 4 to sneak past it. Hmm\u2026 what to do, what to do\u2026)<br /> <br /> You can't have it both ways: it can't be \u201cthe Gauntlet is so thin or non-existent past the Spatial Horizon that mages spontaneously fall through it\u201d <i>and</i> \u201cmages can pass the Spatial Horizon in normal space without any difficulty\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T21:43:00-07:00","id":1263162,"title":"","content":"Well that is why I\u2019m asking, because there is a few ways to handle it, like goi g up on a rocket knocks Mages into the Umbra but not across the Barrier if they try. Or the gauntlet is thin but you only go to the Near Realm of the Aetherial realm if you pass.<br /> <br /> Really simple.<br /> <br /> To access the Magy stuff you need to pierce those membranes. This works as Garou can walk to the Aetherial Realm and find Anchorheads to enter the Deep Umbra. Maybe going into space is a shortcut to just the Aetherial Realm, with planets possessing gates on their Umbra domains to all that wonky mage realms. Rage Across the Heavens even talks about this were you have to decide if you want Space to have a Penumbra that is just close to the Aetherial Realm or just have the Aetherial Realm as it\u2019s Penumbra. That is really what I am talking about here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T01:26:01-07:00","id":1263169,"title":"","content":"Note that the Aethereal Realms are effectively still in the Earth's atmosphere: they're Near Umbra, and in Werewolf (and pre-Revised Mage) cosmology, the Near Umbra ends at the edge of Earth's atmosphere. Basically, the Aethereal Realms are kind of like the Shade Realms: the Aethereal Realm of Helios isn't the Celestine Helios; like all Celestines, Helios resides in what werewolves consider to be the Deep Umbra. <br /> <br /> (As of Revised, mages split the Werewolf Deep Umbra into two parts: Etherspace, which extends out to roughly the asteroid belt and coexists with regular space; and the Void, which extends outward from the asteroid belt and either absorbs regular space or replaces it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T02:06:14-07:00","id":1263171,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know if werewolf acknowledges the wacky mage spaceumbra at all. They do talk about the optional idea of the Aetherial Realm being the space Penumbra in Rage Across the Heavens. I don\u2019t remember seeing anything about going to Pluto requiring Membrane crossing.<br /> <br /> Yes the Aetherial Realm is near Umbra, more a home for Incarnae rather then Celestine\u2019s. But it can tap into Celestine\u2019s but that requires communion with their Incarna and most planets Celestine\u2019s are Sleeping or Dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T02:51:36-07:00","id":1263174,"title":"","content":"The Aethereal Realms don't require crossing the Membrane; that's why I said that they're more like Shade Realms \u2014 though I meant to say \u201cas opposed to Shard Realms\u201d. <br /> <br /> And no, Werewolf doesn't really acknowledge Mage's \u201cspace Umbra\u201d\u2026 because werewolves rarely leave Earth. The farthest they usually venture is the aforementioned Aethereal Realms; and when they <i>do</i> go beyond the Membrane, it's usually by means of the shortcuts that the Aethereal Realms provide \u2014 meaning that they rarely enter Mage's Etherspace. Heck, aside from Void Engineers and the occasional Etherite, <i>mages</i> rarely venture out into Etherspace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-28-2018, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T15:23:45-08:00","id":1264811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1261337-i-thought-they-abandoned-the-whole-space-is-the-umbra-thing?p=1263171#post1263171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know if werewolf acknowledges the wacky mage spaceumbra at all. They do talk about the optional idea of the Aetherial Realm being the space Penumbra in Rage Across the Heavens. I don\u2019t remember seeing anything about going to Pluto requiring Membrane crossing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there was some stuff in some book about the Russian space station Mir containing a portal to Malfeas - GttTech briefly mentions Void Engineers fighting (and defeating) BSDs there. I think that's as close as it gets to the Garou interacting with either Conventional space or etherspace on a wide level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 11-05-2018, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}